.TH UFW-GUARD 8 "November 2026" "ufw-guard 0.5.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ufw-guard \- enforce audit comments on UFW firewall rules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ufw
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ufw-guard
provides the
.B ufw
command as a governance wrapper. Rule creation commands are checked for a valid audit comment before the original UFW program runs. Other commands pass through to UFW.
.SH RULE COMMANDS
The wrapper enforces comments on
.BR allow , deny , reject , limit , route , insert ,
and
.BR prepend .
Supply a reason using
.BR comment :
.PP
.B ufw allow 22/tcp comment "Allow SSH ingress"
.PP
If the comment is missing, an interactive terminal prompts for one. A non-interactive invocation without a comment fails with an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --force-no-comment
Bypass comment enforcement for this invocation. The flag is removed before calling UFW. This bypass is unavailable when
.B allow_bypass = false
is set in the configuration file.
.TP
.B --audit
Report existing firewall rules that lack valid comments. Exit status 2 means non-compliant rules were found.
.TP
.B --remediate
Interactively add comments to existing rules that lack them.
.TP
.B --help, -h
Display help.
.TP
.B --version, -v
Display version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UFW_GUARD_BYPASS
Set to
.B 1
or
.B true
to bypass comment enforcement, unless bypass is disabled in configuration.
.TP
.B UFW_GUARD_CONFIG
Use an alternate configuration file instead of
.IR /etc/ufw/ufw-guard.conf .
.TP
.B UFW_GUARD_NON_INTERACTIVE
Disable interactive prompts when set to
.BR 1 .
.TP
.B UFW_GUARD_UPSTREAM_PATH
Select the path of the upstream UFW executable.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The optional
.I /etc/ufw/ufw-guard.conf
file controls
.BR allow_bypass , min_comment_length , comment_pattern , require_comment_on_delete ,
and
.BR auto_append_user .
See
the project README for examples.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ufw/ufw-guard.conf
Optional system policy.
.TP
.I /usr/local/sbin/ufw
Installed governance wrapper.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/ufw
Upstream UFW program, unless overridden by
.BR UFW_GUARD_UPSTREAM_PATH .
.SH SECURITY
The bypass flag and environment variable are intended for emergency use. Disable bypass in system configuration for strict environments. Comments are audit metadata and do not replace firewall access controls.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ufw (8)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/jericbas/ufw-guard/issues.
